# Generated by python -m ridge.deck_narrative --write. Scenario wording is
# rendered from assets/scenario-narrative-v1.json; do not retype it here.
pageType: content
audience: participant
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$paper"
elements:
  - elementId: tag
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 40, 400, 16]
    content: {style: "$tag", wrap: false, text: PART 2 · HOW THE DAY WORKS — PHASE 2 OF 4}
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 66, 528, 31]
    contractRef: phases.phase-2.title
    content: {style: "$title", fontSize: 27, wrap: false, text: The workstation that sent it}
  - elementId: rule
    elementType: line
    bounds: [64, 116, 832, 2]
    viewBox: [832, 2]
    points: "0,1.0 832,1.0"
    curve: sharp
    border: {style: solid, width: 2, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: tickets-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [600, 64, 296, 14]
    content: {fontSize: 11, bold: true, color: "$amber", wrap: false, align: [right, top], text: TICKETS IN THIS PHASE}
  - elementId: tickets
    elementType: text
    bounds: [600, 82, 296, 16]
    contractRef: phases.phase-2.tickets
    content: {fontSize: 13, bold: true, color: "$slate", align: [right, top], text: T04 · T05 · T13 · T14 · T15 · T16 · T17 · T18}
  - elementId: timeframe
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 128, 832, 17]
    contractRef: phases.phase-2.timeframe
    content: {style: "$small", wrap: false, text: "The longest phase, and the one that rewards patience"}
  - elementId: purpose-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 166, 396, 19]
    content: {fontSize: 15, bold: true, color: "$slate", wrap: false, text: PURPOSE}
  - elementId: purpose-rule
    elementType: line
    bounds: [64, 193, 396, 2]
    viewBox: [396, 2]
    points: "0,1.0 396,1.0"
    curve: sharp
    border: {style: solid, width: 2, color: "$slate"}
  - elementId: purpose
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 205, 396, 67]
    contractRef: phases.phase-2.purpose
    content:
      style: "$body"
      fontSize: 14
      text: |
        <p>Establish what was on the host: what arrived, what persisted, what was cached, and what the prepared records and the training surrogate can and cannot tell you.</p>
  - elementId: urgency-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [500, 166, 396, 19]
    content: {fontSize: 15, bold: true, color: "$amber", wrap: false, text: URGENCY}
  - elementId: urgency-rule
    elementType: line
    bounds: [500, 193, 396, 2]
    viewBox: [396, 2]
    points: "0,1.0 396,1.0"
    curve: sharp
    border: {style: solid, width: 2, color: "$amber"}
  - elementId: urgency
    elementType: text
    bounds: [500, 205, 396, 67]
    contractRef: phases.phase-2.urgency
    content:
      style: "$body"
      fontSize: 14
      text: |
        <p>Steady. This is the phase where teams either build a coherent account or collect isolated facts. Slow is fine; scattershot is not.</p>
  - elementId: action-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 304, 832, 16]
    content: {fontSize: 13, bold: true, color: "$amber", wrap: false, text: WHAT YOU DO HERE}
  - elementId: action-rule
    elementType: line
    bounds: [64, 326, 832, 2]
    viewBox: [832, 2]
    points: "0,1.0 832,1.0"
    curve: sharp
    border: {style: solid, width: 2, color: "$amber"}
  - elementId: action
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 338, 832, 47]
    contractRef: phases.phase-2.action
    content:
      style: "$body"
      fontSize: 15
      text: |
        <p>Recover the cache, read the prepared native records with their provenance, and inspect the surrogate statically. Keep static findings labelled as static.</p>
  - elementId: transition-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 395, 832, 16]
    content: {fontSize: 13, bold: true, color: "$amber", wrap: false, text: AND THEN}
  - elementId: transition-rule
    elementType: line
    bounds: [64, 417, 832, 2]
    viewBox: [832, 2]
    points: "0,1.0 832,1.0"
    curve: sharp
    border: {style: solid, width: 2, color: "$amber"}
  - elementId: transition
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 429, 832, 44]
    contractRef: phases.phase-2.transition
    content:
      style: "$body"
      fontSize: 14
      text: |
        <p>A program is on the host and something left the network. The remaining question is whether the account that was used was ever really locked down.</p>
  - elementId: footer
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 505, 700, 15]
    content: {fontSize: 12, color: "#7E877F", wrap: false, text: OPERATION SILENT RIDGE — EXERCISE ONLY}
  - elementId: pagenum
    elementType: text
    bounds: [880, 505, 40, 15]
    content: {fontSize: 12, color: "#7E877F", align: [right, top], wrap: false, text: "9"}
